+# Recording backend host tests
+
+Run `sh tests/recording/test.sh` from the sensorfw root, or invoke that script by
+its absolute path from elsewhere. Requires a Linux host and a C++17 compiler with
+ASan/UBSan and GNU-compatible linker wrapping. Set `CXX` to select the compiler.
+No Qt build, vendor libraries, root access or watch connection is needed.
+
+The suite checks:
+
+- Raw queue order, overflow accounting and preservation of unread records.
+- UI/recorder demand arbitration, rollback and control-result validation.
+- Segment rotation, checkpoint publication, finalization and failed writes.
+- Worker backpressure, asynchronous errors and capture-directory reuse refusal.
+- Durable record counts while fsync is blocked or fails, including later arrivals.
+- Storage admission and runtime free-space reserve failures.
+
+These are standalone component tests. They do not establish live HAL behavior,
+Qt event-loop integration, physical sensor continuity or suspend correctness.
+Build outputs stay in the ignored `build/` directory; fixtures use temporary
+directories and never open the production recording socket or power sysfs files.
+
+The initial tests were preserved from asteroid-watch tasks 0220 (queue, demand,
+control, storage and worker), 0226 (durability watermark) and 0235 (space reserve).
+Those historical task copies remain unchanged; maintain future regressions here.
